2. HOW THE RELEASE WORKS
   (CONTRACT MECHANICS)

    1. Submit the closeout
       packet - punch-list
       sign-off, as-builts,
       warranties - through
       the owner's project
       office (the contact
       on the contract's
       front page, reached
       at the numbers in
       the notice clause).
    2. Lien waiver exchange
       follows the contract's
       clause: a CONDITIONAL
       waiver accompanies
       the final payment
       application; the
       unconditional form
       is exchanged only
       AFTER funds are in
       your account. That
       order protects both
       sides and is the
       industry standard -
       any "waiver first,
       wire later to a new
       escrow" flow reverses
       a protection into a
       trap.
    3. Payment releases to
       the account of record
       - the same account
       every progress
       payment used.
       Account changes, if
       ever needed, follow
       the contract's
       change procedure:
       written notice,
       verification call
       to your known
       contacts, and a
       documented cooldown -
       never banking
       details embedded in
       a release email.

  The Owner's project office
  will NEVER:
  - Introduce a "new escrow
    coordinator" (a Delaware
    LLC receiving final
    payments "first, then
    forwarding") - funds
    that leave for an
    unknown intermediary
    are funds gone; the
    "lender's requirement"
    framing is the standard
    furniture of
    retainage-fraud emails
  - Demand the
    unconditional lien
    waiver BEFORE payment
    (conditional-then-
    unconditional is the
    AIA sequence precisely
    to prevent waiver-
    first theft)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "projectone-or" or
    "po-retainage"

